      "affectedParagraphs": [
        {
          "index": 8,
          "blockIndex": 8,
          "paragraphInBlock": 0,
          "text": "The motion-induced effective force acts along conductor $AB$. For the EMF calculation, integrate the effective force in (12-5) over the charge's displacement $l$ relative to the conductor:"
        },
        {
          "index": 9,
          "blockIndex": 9,
          "paragraphInBlock": 0,
          "text": "$A=f\\cdot l=|q|vBl\\sin\\alpha$."
        },
        {
          "index": 10,
          "blockIndex": 9,
          "paragraphInBlock": 1,
          "text": "Here A is the effective-force integral for motion relative to the conductor, not the total magnetic work on a carrier. The magnetic force is perpendicular to the carrier's total velocity, including motion with and within the conductor, so it does no total work on the carrier."
        },
        {
          "index": 11,
          "blockIndex": 10,
          "paragraphInBlock": 0,
          "text": "The external mechanical agent maintaining the motion of conductor $AB$ supplies the electrical energy. The induced EMF is the conductor-relative effective-force integral per unit charge magnitude:"
        },
        {
          "index": 13,
          "blockIndex": 12,
          "paragraphInBlock": 0,
          "text": "This formula applies to a straight conductor moving at speed $v$ in a uniform magnetic field and having length $l$, under the geometric conditions above. The rod lies along v cross B, perpendicular to both v and B; alpha is the angle between v and B."
        }
      ],
